# M5GFX's hosted SDL renderer swaps and reads its double-buffer pointer
# on different threads. Furble does not own that backend; suppress only its
# frames so the focused GPS scenario still reports races in Furble code.
race:lgfx::v1::Panel_sdl

# SDL teardown reaches libdbus through Panel_sdl::close(), and dbus takes its
# own connection and dispatch locks in one order there and the other order
# during setup. Every frame in the report is inside libdbus-1.so; furble owns
# neither lock and cannot order them. Match the module rather than
# lgfx::v1::Panel_sdl so an inversion with a furble frame still fails the gate.
deadlock:libdbus-1.so
